WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.120
When Alexander Graham Bell invented the telephone in 1876, he designed it to do one thing.

2
00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:14.160
Make phone calls.

3
00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:17.520
These days it seems we use our phones for everything but phone calls.

4
00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:22.440
Today's phones are our text messengers, calculators, books, planners, navigators,

5
00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:27.940
our cameras, music players, internet browsers, stock traders, even our flashlights.

6
00:00:27.940 --> 00:00:32.180
These evolved to include so many other useful features because we needed them to.

7
00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:34.460
Yet we still just call them phones.

8
00:00:34.460 --> 00:00:38.340
This same evolution by necessity has happened with other products over the years,

9
00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:40.460
and life insurance is no exception.

10
00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:45.540
When life insurance was invented way back in the 1600s, it was also designed to do one thing.

11
00:00:45.540 --> 00:00:49.740
To financially protect your loved ones when your life is over.

12
00:00:49.740 --> 00:00:53.420
And like phones, life insurance evolved because we needed it to.

13
00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:57.300
With modern advancements in medicine, suffering a critical illness like a heart attack,

14
00:00:57.300 --> 00:01:01.700
stroke, or cancer diagnosis no longer necessarily means death.

15
00:01:01.700 --> 00:01:06.780
In fact, 90% of people who suffer a heart attack these days survive that event.

16
00:01:06.780 --> 00:01:10.460
That's where the new, evolved kind of life insurance policy comes in.

17
00:01:10.460 --> 00:01:12.460
One that adds living benefits.

18
00:01:12.460 --> 00:01:16.580
Living benefits policies are essentially the smartphones of life insurance.

19
00:01:16.580 --> 00:01:20.180
They allow your life insurance policy to not just be a parting gift,

20
00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:24.900
but also provide the ability to accelerate the death benefit if you suffer a critical,

21
00:01:24.900 --> 00:01:26.620
chronic, or terminal illness.

22
00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:31.580
This ability can help save your financial life by unlocking a whole new list of ways

23
00:01:31.580 --> 00:01:34.660
to use your policy while you're still living.

24
00:01:34.660 --> 00:01:39.580
And oftentimes, it does all of this at the same price as the old kind of life insurance.

25
00:01:39.580 --> 00:01:42.860
Living benefits protect you, your loved ones, and your wallet,

26
00:01:42.860 --> 00:01:46.980
not only in case you die, but also in case you don't.

27
00:01:46.980 --> 00:01:50.820
Two things always happen when you suffer a critical or chronic illness.

28
00:01:50.820 --> 00:01:54.460
Your expenses go up, and your income goes down.

29
00:01:54.460 --> 00:01:59.300
When your expenses get higher than your income, that's when debt begins to pile up.

30
00:01:59.300 --> 00:02:04.100
This is the exact trap that so many Americans are falling into every single day.

31
00:02:04.100 --> 00:02:07.940
In fact, 60% of all bankruptcies that occur in the U.S.

32
00:02:07.940 --> 00:02:12.100
are the direct result of a critical illness and the medical expenses that follow.

33
00:02:12.100 --> 00:02:16.340
With living benefits, the policyholder has the option to accelerate a portion

34
00:02:16.340 --> 00:02:20.940
of their death benefit to replace their income and help with those added expenses.

35
00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:24.140
These benefits are the difference between just surviving the illness

36
00:02:24.140 --> 00:02:26.140
and having a life afterwards.

37
00:02:26.140 --> 00:02:29.740
And the best part is, they come at no extra cost to the consumer.

38
00:02:29.740 --> 00:02:32.380
So what kind of life insurance is protecting your family?

39
00:02:32.380 --> 00:02:34.780
Your granddad's traditional death benefit only coverage?

40
00:02:34.780 --> 00:02:36.340
I don't know if I'm hearing anything.

41
00:02:36.340 --> 00:02:40.100
Or the new, evolved life insurance with built-in living benefits?

42
00:02:40.100 --> 00:02:42.780
If you're still using the rotary phone of life insurance,

43
00:02:42.780 --> 00:02:46.460
maybe it's time for an upgrade.

44
00:02:46.460 --> 00:02:48.900
Contact the person that shared this video with you to find out

45
00:02:48.900 --> 00:02:51.100
how you can add living benefits to your coverage.
